# Vendored dev tool — single source of truth in Mentat/tools/attr-audit
# (installed via `node install.mjs`; do not reformat or it drifts from the template)
scripts/attr-audit.mjs

# Generated lockfiles — pnpm owns their format. Prettier reformatting them
# (via lint-staged's `*` glob) produces a spurious full-file diff and drifts
# them from what `pnpm install` writes. Matches root + workspace (documentation/).
pnpm-lock.yaml

# TODS fixtures — deliberately NOT prettier's business, and not merely ungated.
# verify.yml already records why they are outside `format:check`: reformatting them is a
# ~40k-line diff across large test corpora that buries their blame for no benefit. But that
# only excused the GATE. lint-staged's `*` glob was still free to reformat one the moment
# anybody staged it for an unrelated reason, and the 40k-line argument applies with full
# force to whichever fixture that happened to be. Ignoring them closes it for good.
**/*.tods.json

# Generated by release-please on every release. Formatting it means fighting the generator:
# the next generated write reverts whatever prettier did, so the file would oscillate.
CHANGELOG.md
